  (text "R1006 on 01-power is the local 22.1k SHDN pull-down. Open contact = electronic OFF.\n100nF is an edge filter, not a guaranteed debounce circuit. SHDN cycling clears a latched fault.\nFoinse-fed use: retain a deliberate closed Croi enable plug, or add an independent third switch pole.\nUSB may still power service logic. Unplug the battery for storage. Not physical energetic isolation."
    (at 15.24 177.8 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "fc65c2e9-7074-4256-ae08-a5c1650f4128"))
  (text "What this does: Lets an external maintained switch turn Croi's battery path on and off, without carrying load current through the switch.\nConnects to: J103 pin 1 is a limited 3 V bias; pin 2 returns to the eFuse SHDN input on 01-power. Open/unplugged means electronic OFF, not physical disconnection."
    (at 15.24 27.94 0.0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.4 1.4))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid "d383a0df-4709-5bf5-8ea7-0b5c0dd8e7d6")))
